Everyone talks about how he finished, how he died, or how to progress past
______, so here's something different. I'm curious if others start nethack
the way I do. Having completed older versions of the game before, I tend to
throw caution to the wind at the beginning. I drink most potions, read most
scrolls and books, and zap most wands -- without identifying them. I typically
fight monsters without watching to see how close to death I am. If I make it
to the mines, I start to be a little more cautious. Usually, at this point, I
have already identified several items and know what my chances are on new ones.

How do you start?

